  // design: Flavius Rule's octagon (docs/map-briefs/sandfall_colosseum/OCTAGON_PLAN.md): made by tools/content/kit/arenaCorner.mjs. The anchor cell is the corner of the sand (the tile covers the cells 0..8 east and north of it). The rows are the Seating Tier's (0.5 m by 1 m) and the podium Arena Seating's, so they meet the straight bays flush; seats in the solids slot, lips in trim, walls and vaults in walls, walkways and slabs in floor. Arches collide plain (piers and lintel; owner 2026-11-14, 6a). The gate option (phase 3, MapMaker's tile inspector: a tile of its own, so maps need no new field): a Gladiator Gate on the diagonal (passage 3.2 m wide and 3 m clear under the gatehouse, where a portcullis hangs 1 m in from the podium's face, then 3.4 m through the fill), out through the facade's middle arch; a stair well either side of it from the passage down to level -1, whose foot landing meets the north side (and, mirrored, the east side) of tile cell 2, 2, -1, the hypogeum ring's corner, through a 3.6 m opening; a short stair of eight steps up the podium wall either side of the mouth, open with the portcullis down (owner 4b). The wells hang a level under the tile's cells (no cell at level -1 is claimed: put the hypogeum's tunnels there); its bore takes the ground out round them.
